    Bug 1999601 - Fix intermittent timeout in test_save_eml_as_file2 by correcting window focus and mock contexts. r=mkmelin


    The `test_save_eml_as_file2` test intermittently timed out waiting for
    the MockFilePicker promise to resolve. This was caused by two intertwined
    issues:

    1. Window Focus Race: The test synthesized the `Ctrl+S` save shortcut
    immediately after the `msgLoaded` condition. On slower runners, the OS
    had not yet granted keyboard focus to the new window (`msgc2`), causing
    the keystroke to miss. This is fixed by awaiting `SimpleTest.promiseFocus(msgc2)`.

    2. Misaligned Mock Context: The `MockFilePicker` was being initialized on
    the main window's browsing context (`window.browsingContext`) instead of
    the new message window's context (`msgc2.browsingContext`). When the focus
    fix above routed the keystroke correctly to `msgc2`, it triggered a native
    OS file dialog, hanging the test. The mock is now correctly bound to the
    secondary window.
    The test intermittently times out waiting for the MockFilePicker promise
    to resolve. This occurs because the test synthesizes the `Ctrl+S` save
    shortcut immediately after the `msgLoaded` condition is met.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286557

